:"2025-09-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"},{"bioguideId":"C001103","fullName":"Rep. Carter, Earl L. \"Buddy\" [R-GA-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-09-15","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"GA"},{"bioguideId":"C001137","fullName":"Rep. Crank, Jeff [R-CO-5]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-10-06","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CO"},{"bioguideId":"T000490","fullName":"Rep. Taylor, David J. [R-OH-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"OH"},{"bioguideId":"C001133","fullName":"Rep. Ciscomani, Juan [R-AZ-6]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-07","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"AZ"},{"bioguideId":"M000871","fullName":"Rep. Mann, Tracey [R-KS-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-10","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KS"},{"bioguideId":"K000403","fullName":"Rep. Kennedy, Mike [R-UT-3]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-11-17","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"UT"},{"bioguideId":"S001228","fullName":"Rep. Schmidt, Derek [R-KS-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2025-12-19","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"KS"},{"bioguideId":"M001205","fullName":"Rep. Miller, Carol D. [R-WV-1]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-14","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"WV"},{"bioguideId":"V000129","fullName":"Rep. Valadao, David G. [R-CA-22]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-01-21","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"CA"},{"bioguideId":"H001091","fullName":"Rep. Hinson, Ashley [R-IA-2]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-02-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"IA"},{"bioguideId":"L000599","fullName":"Rep. Lawler, Michael [R-NY-17]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-04-20","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"NY"},{"bioguideId":"S000250","fullName":"Rep. Sessions, Pete [R-TX-17]","isOriginalCosponsor":false,"party":"R","sponsorshipDate":"2026-06-09","sponsorshipWithdrawnDate":null,"state":"TX"}],"fetchedAt":"2026-09-20T14:05:39+00:00","id":"hr1163-119","introducedDate":"2025-02-10","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2026-05-04","text":"Placed on the Union Calendar, Calendar No. 552."},"laws":[],"number":"1163","originChamber":"House","policyArea":"Government Operations and Politics","sponsors":[{"bioguideId":"F000475","district":1,"fullName":"Rep. Finstad, Brad [R-MN-1]","party":"R","state":"MN"}],"summaries":[{"actionDate":"2025-02-10","actionDesc":"Introduced in House","text":"<p><strong>Prove It Act of 2025</strong></p><p>This bill expands the requirements for federal agency rulemaking with respect to small businesses, organizations, and governmental jurisdictions.</p><p>Specifically, when conducting an initial regulatory flexibility analysis, agencies must include, where feasible, any reasonably foreseeable indirect costs the proposed rule may impose on small entities.</p><p>Further, if an agency certifies that an initial regulatory flexibility analysis is not required because the rule will not have a significant economic impact on a substantial number of small entities, the agency must provide such certification within 10 days to the Office of Advocacy of the Small Business Administration. A small entity or group of small entities may petition the Office of Advocacy to review such certification. The petition must include specified information, such as the issues the petitioner believes should be addressed and a proposed solution to the issues raised.</p><p>If the Office of Advocacy ultimately determines, upon a full review of the petition, that the proposed rule would have a significant economic impact on a&nbsp;substantial number of small entities, the agency promulgating the rule must perform an initial&nbsp;and final regulatory flexibility analysis for the rule. Additionally, if the agency does not participate or assist in the full review process, the finalized rule shall not apply to small entities.</p><p>The bill also requires agencies to publish, and allow for comments on, all guidance documents with respect to any rule an agency determines is likely to have a significant economic impact on a substantial number of small entities.</p>","updateDate":"2026-06-11T18:51:57Z","versionCode":"00"}],"title":"Prove It Act","type":"hr","updateDate":"2026-09-19T23:31:21Z","updateDateIncludingText":"2026-09-19T23:31:21Z"}
